Show the declaring file before the symbol in the -v table, and make recompiling stable by reusing imported variable addresses

With no source file, `axy -v` now lists each symbol as `filename: name` (e.g. `lib.axy: score = $70`) — the declaring file comes first, before the symbol — instead of appending it after.

A variable already present in the imported `.axysymbols` table now keeps its recorded address instead of being allocated a fresh one. Only new variables are taken from the counter (and advance it), so recompiling a file no longer shifts or skips variable addresses and the state file stays stable.

